      "body": "\r\n\r\n\r\n## Purpose\r\n\r\nHi! I'm new to vLLM and starting from good first issues. While looking at\r\n#28407, I found the DCP error message was already improved in #40053 — but\r\nthe neighboring **MTP** and **PCP** assertions in\r\n`check_attention_cp_compatibility` still raise bare errors with no hint on\r\nhow to recover. This PR gives them the same actionable style:\r\n\r\n- **MTP**: suggest `--cp-kv-cache-interleave-size 1` or disabling speculative decoding.\r\n- **PCP**: suggest disabling via `--prefill-context-parallel-size 1`.\r\n\r\nNote: no backend currently sets `supports_pcp`, so the PCP hint only\r\nsuggests disabling it rather than switching backends.\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\n\r\nError-message-only change, no behavioral impact.\r\n\r\n## Test Result\r\n\r\nN/A — only assertion message text changed.\r\n\r\n---\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Essential Elements of an Effective PR Description Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [ ] The purpose of the PR, such as \"Fix some issue (link existing issues this PR will resolve)\".\r\n- [ ] The test plan, such as providing test command.\r\n- [ ] The test results, such as pasting the results comparison before and after, or e2e results\r\n- [ ] (Optional) The necessary documentation update, such as updating `supported_models.md` and `examples` for a new model.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n",
